course: dictionary
lesson: 9394
title: Sprinkle: scattering small bits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To sprinkle something is to scatter small drops or bits over it, like salt, sugar, water or seeds. The clues are in the sentence: «Grit or sand sprinkled on an icy path gives shoes more grip.» Grit and sand are tiny bits spread across the ice, so sprinkled means scattered over the path.
explain: Sprinkle can also be a noun. A sprinkle is a small amount scattered, and sprinkles are tiny coloured sugar pieces on cakes and ice cream. Try the swap test: put "scattered over in small bits" in place of sprinkled, and «Grit or sand scattered over an icy path gives shoes more grip» still makes sense.
explain: Sprinkle has a weather meaning too. «It's sprinkling» means it is raining lightly, with just a few small drops rather than a downpour. Scientists also sprinkle things to see patterns: «Iron filings sprinkled around a magnet line up and show its invisible magnetic field.»
fact: To sprinkle means to scatter small drops or bits over something.
fact: A sprinkle is a small amount scattered.
fact: Sprinkles are tiny coloured sugar pieces for decorating cakes and ice cream.
fact: «It's sprinkling» means it is raining lightly.
fact: Phrases you will meet: «sprinkle with», «a sprinkle of», «rainbow sprinkles».
exercise: «Grit or sand sprinkled on an icy path gives shoes more grip.» What does sprinkled mean here? | *Scattered over in small bits | Cleaned off with a brush | Frozen into one big block | Thrown in a single heap
exercise: Mia says «It's sprinkling» means the park sprinklers are on. What does it really mean? | It is windy and cold | The park sprinklers are switched on | It is very hot and sunny | *It is raining lightly
exercise: In «a sprinkle of cheese on the pizza», what kind of word is sprinkle? | *A noun, meaning a small amount | A colour | A place | A verb, meaning an action
test: «Iron filings sprinkled around a magnet line up and show its invisible magnetic field.» What do the filings show? | The colour of the magnet | How hot the magnet is | *The hidden pattern of the magnetic field | Bits of metal too heavy to move
test: Which sentence uses sprinkle as a verb? | *Sprinkle pepper on the soup | A sprinkle of sugar is on the cake | There was a sprinkle at lunch | Rainbow sprinkles are my favourite
exam: A cook says «sprinkle the cheese on top». Which phrase is the best swap for sprinkle? | Count every piece of | Wrap a big block around | *Scatter small bits over | Melt into a puddle on
